<section class="ceo-decision" aria-label="Investment committee recommendation">
<h3>My investment decision</h3>
<p><strong>Vendor-first, with hybrid as a challenger.</strong> Glean provisionally scores 3.20/5 versus hybrid 3.15/5 and custom build 2.55/5. The difference is too small for a vendor commitment; the scores are assumptions to validate.</p>
<div class="ceo-view-buttons" role="group" aria-label="Explore the CEO decision">
<button type="button" class="is-selected" data-ceo-view="recommendation" aria-pressed="true">My recommendation</button>
<button type="button" data-ceo-view="challenge" aria-pressed="false">CEO challenges me</button>
</div>
<div class="ceo-view" data-ceo-panel="recommendation"><p>Fund a focused evaluation of the vendor route against improved search, with a small hybrid feasibility spike only if integration or scientific workflow gaps justify it. Do not approve a custom product yet.</p></div>
<div class="ceo-view" data-ceo-panel="challenge" hidden><blockquote>“Why shouldn't we build something we own? Our science is unique.”</blockquote><p>I would own the scientific capability that makes us different, not automatically the entire software stack. Our illustrative custom model carries €3.30m three-year expense versus €2.70m gross capacity value—not cash savings. Building merits investment only if research evidence reveals a recurring differentiated workflow that vendors cannot serve economically.</p></div>
<p class="scenario-note">The €80–150k estimate is for the existing eight-week pilot scope. Evaluating two full implementations would require a revised estimate and approval.</p>
</section>
